module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.generic_optional_over_a_type_application_argument_loses_the_optional

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data generic_optional_over_a_type_application_argument_loses_the_optional: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "generic_optional_over_a_type_application_argument_loses_the_optional" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**CLASS: a pattern binding of a generic optional `T?` is typed `T`, not `T?`, when `T` is instantiated with a TYPE APPLICATION -- an alias such as `Nat` (= `CommutativeSemiring<Magnitude>`) or a generic record such as `CohortSeatReading<K>`.** Primitive arguments (`Int`, `String`) and bare type parameters keep the optional. INVALID STATE: with `type StaircaseOutcome<L, S> = StaircaseStopped { last_sustained: L?, stop: S } | ...` (std.staircase), `match o { StaircaseStopped { last_sustained: l, stop: _ } => match l { Absent => true Present { value: _ } => false } _ => false }` over `o: StaircaseOutcome<Nat, S>` refuses at resolve with `dag/std/nat.dag:7:12: error: variant 'Absent' not found in type 'Nat'` (and the same for Present). `Nat` is the alias `CommutativeSemiring<Magnitude>`. The error is located at the alias declaration, not the use site.",

    "CONTROLS (2026-09-29, claim_batch at /cargo-target/release/claim_batch built 2026-09-29T04:12). The identical match over `StaircaseOutcome<Int, S>` PASSES. `run_staircase` over Nat levels that completes, matched on `StaircaseCompleted { last_sustained: l } => l == ...`, PASSES. A generic record `Holder<L> { last: L? }` at `Holder<Nat>` matched directly on a function parameter PASSES. The same `Holder<Nat>` reached through an outer constructor's field pattern (`OuterHas { inner: Holder { last: l } }`) FAILS with the same error. Repros were written as throwaway witness files by proud-wolf-311 and handed to the compiler lane the parent dispatched for the fix.",

    "SECOND SIGHTING, WHICH WIDENED THE CLASS (2026-09-29, product.capacity.cohort_observation on gunbc#12689's branch): `first_duplicate_by_key(xs: seats, key: ...)` with `seats: List<CohortSeatReading<K>>` returns `T?`, and `match ... { Present { value: d } => ... d.seat ... }` refused with `variant 'Present' not found in type 'CohortSeatReading'`, located at the parameter's declared type, not the match. No alias is involved, so the row's first name (`generic_optional_field_over_an_alias_argument_loses_the_optional`) named too narrow a class and was renamed before landing. That module is written with single-pass folds over sum-typed accumulators that never wrap a seat record in an optional, which is also its cheaper shape, so it carries no workaround to retire.",

    "HARM: an author who meets this refuses nothing typed. The error names a std declaration the author did not touch, so the natural reading is that the edit broke `std.nat`; the natural move is to reshape the caller until the error goes away. proud-wolf-311 spent three resolve cycles restructuring V4.1 production code on a wrong theory of the defect before bisecting it. A workaround that binds the value through a function parameter declared `L?` resolves, which hides the deficit if it is not named.",

    "WORKAROUND RETIRED: test.claim.spark.v41_capacity_measurement_witness `w_nothing_sustained(l: Nat?)` is deleted and `the_signed_policy_records_ttft_at_262k_without_stopping_on_it` matches `last_sustained` inline, which is what this row's SUFFICIENT FOR named.",

    "ROOT CAUSE, READ RATHER THAN FITTED (neat-pike-685, 2026-09-30). v1 does not wrap an optional: `L?` is the slot's type node carrying `return_cardinality: CardOptional { layers: OneLayer }` (v1.parse maybe_optional). Generic substitution replaced a bare slot WHOLESALE with its argument node -- v1.compiler.infer substitute_generics_apply (both the TypeVariable arm and the bare-name arm) and v1.compiler.resolve substitute_type_slots_scoped (both the bound type-variable arm and the bare-slot arm) returned the argument as it stood, so the slot's cardinality was replaced by the argument's own. The pattern subject then reached expand_scrut_type_for_variant_lookup as the argument, not as an optional, and Present/Absent were looked up among the argument's variants. THE WRONG LOCATION IS THE SAME DEFECT SEEN TWICE: the substituted node is the argument's node, which for an alias is its declaration, and VariantNotFound took its span from the scrutinee type node -- hence dag/std/nat.dag:7:12. REPAIR: all four arms return preserve_outer_optional_cardinality(outer: slot, inner: argument), the existing single authority for carrying an outer cardinality onto an inner type node; and lookup_variant_in_type takes the use site (the match arm, or the field binding for a nested pattern), so a refused variant is located at the pattern that names it.",

    "WHY PRIMITIVES LOOKED IMMUNE IS NOT ESTABLISHED. The nested Holder<Int> shape passed before the fix and passes after it, but this lane did not isolate which route keeps an Int argument's optional; the row does not claim to know. CORRECTION TO THE CONTROLS ABOVE: on the unfixed seed (main at cfb3e3667a), `fn direct(h: Holder<Nat>) -> Bool { match h { Holder { last: l } => match l { Present ... Absent ... } } }` -- the optional field bound by a pattern on a declared parameter -- REFUSED with the same diagnostic; the direct control that passed was a different shape. The trigger is the type-application argument, not the nesting.",

    "MEASURED BOTH WAYS on one tree, `gunbc run --function probe` over five throwaway fixtures: unfixed seed -- nested Holder<Nat> refused, direct Holder<Nat> refused, `wrap<T>(x: T) -> T?` over Box<Int> refused (`variant 'Present' not found in type 'Box'`), nested Holder<Int> accepted. Fixed seed (regenerated by claim_executor --regen-round-cost until rebuild_packages=0) -- all four accepted and evaluated to the arm the value selects. ENROLLED: test.claim.generic_optional_type_application_witness (nested, direct and returned-optional paths at zero VariantNotFound, the Int control, and a non-optional field at the same alias still refusing both arms), and v1 compiler test generic_optional_over_a_type_application_keeps_the_optional (the refusal count AND that every VariantNotFound lands in the using module, not the alias's).",

    "NOT THIS CLASS: tidy-crane-517's gunbc#12630 shape (`refuse<S>(subject: S) -> Admission<S>`, then `Refused { subject: s } => s.program.invocation`) still fails with `error type cascade` on the fixed seed. It involves no optional; it is a separate root and wants its own row.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS versus `list_head_bound_record_element_stays_t`: that class leaves a binder at the unrefined parameter `T`; this one refines `L` to the alias and then drops the `?` wrapper around it, and only for alias arguments -- a primitive argument keeps the optional.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable -- a typed function boundary at the call site. CURRENT RUNG: 2, mechanically preventable -- the three binding paths named by the trigger are repaired at the substitution authority and held by a discriminating witness on the required floor; the location assertion rides the v1 unit-test lane, which is off the merge path (gunbc.rung_drop rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path). CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed, once every route that instantiates a generic type goes through a substitution that carries the slot's cardinality. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: an enumeration of the seed's type-substitution routes, SUFFICIENT FOR showing that no route other than substitute_generics_apply and substitute_type_slots_scoped replaces a slot node wholesale -- this lane repaired the two it found and did not prove the set closed.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
